/T (Strings cannot becompared with ==; strcmp\(a,b\) returns negative, zero or positive by comparing character codes. Capital letters \(65-90\) have smaller codes than small letters \(97-122\), so "Apple" comes before "apple". Swapping names needs three strcpy calls, while sorting an index array moves only integers. After sorting, equal names are neighbours, so duplicates are found by comparing each name with the previous one.)
